## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`options`): This is where the Contentstack SDK Stack is initialized. The options object passed to contentstack.Stack() lacks the live_preview configuration required by the Contentstack SDK to enable CMS live preview. Without it, the Stack never enters live preview mode, so no downstream component can receive draft content updates — the cause, not the symptom.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add a live_preview config block to the options object, reading CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST (and a CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_ENABLE flag) from env. The Contentstack JS SDK accepts live_preview: { enable: boolean, host: string } in the Stack init options. Also add CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST and CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_ENABLE to the destructured env vars at the top of the file (lines 17-24). Then in src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx, the ContentstackProvider must subscribe to Stack.livePreviewQuery / onEntryChange to merge preview data into the content state — but the gating fix is here: without live_preview in options, the SDK never activates preview mode at all.
- **src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx** (`ContentstackProvider`): Even once the Stack is configured for live preview, the provider only accepts static defaultContent and memoizes it once. It must subscribe to the Contentstack SDK's onEntryChange callback (available after live_preview is enabled on the Stack) and update the content state so all 236 consumers of useContent re-render with draft data.
  - **Minimal fix:** Replace the useMemo with useState for content, add a useEffect that calls Stack.livePreviewQuery or subscribes to the onEntryChange callback from the Contentstack SDK, updating the content state on each preview change. Import Stack from services/contentstack. The callback receives the updated entry which should be merged into the existing content object so getContentByKey continues to work for all consumers.


